+### git stale-branches
+
+Returns a list of the local branches whose last commit is older than a date,
+oldest first, with the date of that commit. It is the first step of a branch
+clean-up, and it does not delete anything. The current branch and the main
+branch are never listed.
+
+    $ git stale-branches
+    2025-01-31	feature/login
+    2025-03-02	old-experiment
+
+The date defaults to 3 months ago. An arbitrary date can be specified using
+`git stale-branches -s <date>`, using any date format
+[supported by `git log`][gitlog]. For the same date, a local branch is either
+listed here or by `git active-branches`, never both.
+
+Use `-m` to list only the stale branches that are merged into the main branch,
+or `-u` to list only the ones that are not:
+
+    $ git stale-branches -s 2025-02-15 -m
+    2025-01-31	feature/login
+
